oose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: ditch\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of ditch as a military technology used in warfare.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, was the use of ditches as a military technology present or absent in the warfare strategies of '<polity>'? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: chain\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of chainmail as a military technology used in warfare. We’re using a broad definition of chainmail. Habergeon was the word used to describe the Chinese version and that would qualify as chainmail. Armor that is made of small metal rings linked together in a pattern to form a mesh.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, was chainmail, defined as armor made of small metal rings linked together in a pattern to form a mesh, present or absent as a military technology in the warfare practices of '<polity>'? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '"Variable name": Sacred Text\n"Variable description":  Hindu sacred texts. “The Pudu Mandapa is an example of a mandapa specifically built for the use during a festival when a deity comes out on procession from the temple’s main shrine and stays in the mandapa for a period of a few hours or many days. The expansion in number, size and grandeur of these festival mandapas is a notable feature of Nayaka-period temple architecture. These structures are for the deity both to rest in and to receive worshippers in and their form reflects these purposes.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2729, 'temperature': 0.2})
2026-06-30 11:43:52,157 [INFO] ("Drawing upon the historical context of indigenous writing systems in West Africa, specifically the Vai syllabary (1833) and its subsequent influence on Mande and Kru scripts (e.g., Mende 1921, Kpelle 1935, Bassa 1920-25), which enabled autochthonous literacy, was 'Sacred Text' – defined as religious or spiritual writings produced in these indigenous scripts – present within '<polity>' during the period from <time-start> to <time-end>? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent", None, [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are are history professor writing challenging questions for PhD students.\n\n    Your task is to create a challenging yet well-defined historical exam question based on a variable definition from a historical dataset.\n    Follow the rules below, and return ONLY the final question template, based on the examples provided. \n    \n    1. Begin the question with a concise explanation of the variable's definition, strictly adhering to the provided description, if no description is provided, use the variable name as the basis for the question.\n    2. Ensure all of the following template markers are used:\n        - '<polity>' for polity names (e.g. 'The Papal States')\n        - '<time-start>' and '<time-end>' for temporal scope\n    3. The question should make abundantly clear what the format of the desired response is and that only that response should be given.\n    4. The output must be exactly one question, ensuring that the question is fully complete in its length, and must end with a question mark (?).\n\n    Structure your response with a clear question template.\n    "}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: atlatl\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of atlatl as a military technology used in warfare.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Consider the period from <time-start> to <time-end> in the context of '<polity>'. Was the atlatl, defined as a spear-thro